{
 "about": "What leaves the process (appendix A 1, 2, 6, 34, 51, 52, plan '읽기 허용 목록'). allowlist: a (host, path, query) the request gate must allow or refuse — both cli-side (operations) and inside fetch.js, which must agree; a refused request is never sent. headers: what fetch.js sends per host (no user-agent override: the REPL's own browser UA stands). builds: the request an operation assembles from identifiers alone (callers never pass composed parameters). redirects: whether a domain-address hop may be followed. All ids are synthetic.",
